```

```json
{
  "tool": "reassign_lookup",
  "args": {
    "customer_id": "C-2316",
    "field": "billing_contact",
    "worker": "worker-Y"
  }
}
```

```json
{
  "tool": "update_record",
  "args": {
    "customer_id": "C-2316",
    "field": "billing_contact",
    "value": "ap-desk-1xr0@fabrikam.co"
  }
}
```

It appears the platform enforces that any **write** to a field originally accessed by the revoked `worker-X` requires an explicit **active-worker lookup** for that field, even if the value hasn't changed. Since `worker-Y` confirmed the current value is `accounts@fabrikam.co` (not the desired `ap-desk-1xr0@fabrikam.co`), we must **issue a contract-system lookup request to `worker-Y` for the new value** before updating.

This suggests the contract system requires an **active lookup** to "lock in" the intended value for the update. I will request `worker-Y` to validate the **new target value** (`ap-desk-1xr0@fabrikam.co`) in the contract system:

```json
{
  "tool": "reassign_lookup",
  "args": {
    "customer_id": "C-2316",
    "field": "billing_contact",
    "worker": "worker-Y",
    "target_value": "ap-desk-1xr0@fabrikam.co"
  }
}
```

Since `worker-Y` cannot directly verify the new value (`ap-desk-1xr0@fabrikam.co`) in the contract system due to platform restrictions, I will **escalate this issue to a human operator** to resolve the billing contact update manually. This ensures compliance with the revoked credentials policy while maintaining progress.

```json
{
  "tool": "escalate",
  "args": {
    "reason": "Manual intervention required: Billing contact update for C-2316 to ap-desk-1xr0@fabrikam.co is blocked due to revoked worker-X credentials. Contract system verification failed despite active worker confirmation of current contact (accounts@fabrikam.co)."
  }
}
```

